      "reading": "いんし",
      "reason": "'因子' (inshi) is a much more appropriate and natural translation for the general sense of 'factor' (e.g., 'contributing factor', 'risk factor') in daily life and general contexts. It also covers the mathematical sense of 'factor' (e.g., prime factor), making it a versatile replacement."
